      ],
      "labSlotVenue": [
        "No Lab for this Course",
        ""
      ],
      "instructor": [
        "Dr. Eslavath Rajkumar"
      ],
      "remark": "",
      "Syllabus": "Stress: Meaning and nature of stress, types of stress: Stress, Distress, eustress. Physiological response to stress, Hans Seyle's General Adaptation Syndrome, Transactional theory of stress. Source of Stress: Internal factors, External factors, Systemic factors. Impact of Stress: Physical, Emotional and Behavioural level. Coping: Meaning and definition. Types of coping: A) Adaptive coping styles- Confrontive coping, Planful problem solving, seeking social support, accepting responsibility, positive reappraisal; B) Maladaptive coping styles: Distancing, Escape-Avoidance, Denial, Mental Disengagement. Stress Management techniques: 1.Managing stress through physical skills: Simple Breathing Exercise: Deep Breathing, Exhalation Breathing, Restful Sleep, Pranayama and Yoga, Meditation, Progressive Relaxation. 2. Managing stress through mental skills: Guided Imagery, Ventilate your Feelings, Irrational Thought Control, Reaching the Point of Satiation, The Method of Thought Substitution. 3. Stress Management at the Behavioural Level: SMART Goals, Develop Positive Disposition, Reorientation to Work, Countering the Stress of Indecisiveness, Identification and Monitoring of Stress."
    }
